” it counted in.\",\"reason\":\"Plain-fields detail carried.\"},{\"segment\":\"a18\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"None of those fields is a substitute for the header: a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice, and has written code whose only possible future is to disagree with the gateway it is talking to.\",\"reason\":\"Joined with b18's consequence.\"},{\"segment\":\"b18\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"None of those fields is a substitute for the header: a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice, and has written code whose only possible future is to disagree with the gateway it is talking to.\",\"reason\":\"Consequence carried in merged sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"a19\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused; nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\",\"reason\":\"Dash replaced with semicolon.\"},{\"segment\":\"b19\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused; nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a19.\"},{\"segment\":\"b20\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## How to retry well\",\"reason\":\"Base heading kept for the retry rules.\"},{\"segment\":\"a21\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"There are four rules, and the order they are given in is the order to apply them.\",\"reason\":\"b21's full sentence used for the rules intro.\"},{\"segment\":\"a22\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"1. Honour the header, every time, and do not compute your own wait.\",\"reason\":\"Rule 1 heading merged with b22.\"},{\"segment\":\"b22\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"1. Honour the header, every time, and do not compute your own wait.\",\"reason\":\"Rule 1 heading merged with a22.\"},{\"segment\":\"a23\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic with information the caller cannot see, and the same rule holds on the 503 path, even though the cause of that refusal is entirely different.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b24's different-cause detail.\"},{\"segment\":\"b23\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic with information the caller cannot see, and the same rule holds on the 503 path, even though the cause of that refusal is entirely different.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a23.\"},{\"segment\":\"b24\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic with information the caller cannot see, and the same rule holds on the 503 path, even though the cause of that refusal is entirely different.\",\"reason\":\"503 detail carried in merged sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"a24\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see, and there is no case at all where a guess is the better of the two.\",\"reason\":\"Joined with a25.\"},{\"segment\":\"a25\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see, and there is no case at all where a guess is the better of the two.\",\"reason\":\"Joined with a24.\"},{\"segment\":\"b25\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see, and there is no case at all where a guess is the better of the two.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a24.\"},{\"segment\":\"b26\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see, and there is no case at all where a guess is the better of the two.\",\"reason\":\"Carried by a25's stronger statement.\"},{\"segment\":\"a26\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"2. Retry only what is safe to retry, which is a smaller set than the set of responses that are not a success.\",\"reason\":\"Rule 2 heading merged with b27.\"},{\"segment\":\"b27\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"2. Retry only what is safe to retry, which is a smaller set than the set of responses that are not a success.\",\"reason\":\"Rule 2 heading merged with a26.\"},{\"segment\":\"a27\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path: the platform itself is overloaded.\",\"reason\":\"Adds b28's platform-overloaded gloss.\"},{\"segment\":\"b28\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path: the platform itself is overloaded.\",\"reason\":\"Same four cases, stated once.\"},{\"segment\":\"b29\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a29.\"},{\"segment\":\"b30\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"Avoid writing that loop.\",\"reason\":\"Same instruction as a30.\"},{\"segment\":\"a32\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"A batch credential’s allowance is measured over exactly the same window as the default, not under a separate counting scheme.\",\"reason\":\"'Fifty times' conflicts with 100/1000; explicit 1000 kept, window kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b31\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"A batch credential’s allowance is measured over exactly the same window as the default, not under a separate counting scheme.\",\"reason\":\"1000 carried in intro; '50 times' conflicts and was not kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"a34\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Nothing else about the two tiers differs.\",\"reason\":\"Redundant 'in any way' removed.\"},{\"segment\":\"b33\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"Nothing else about the two tiers differs.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a34.\"},{\"segment\":\"a35\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"4. Log every refusal seen, and keep the log for at least a week.\",\"reason\":\"Rule 4 heading merged with b34's retention.\"},{\"segment\":\"b34\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"4. Log every refusal seen, and keep the log for at least a week.\",\"reason\":\"Retention period carried in rule 4.\"},{\"segment\":\"b35\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused last week cannot argue for a larger cap, and nobody at the far end will assemble that argument on its behalf.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a36.\"},{\"segment\":\"b37\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## Other refusals and their codes\",\"reason\":\"Base heading kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"a39\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Not all refusals are caps.\",\"reason\":\"Subject made explicit.\"},{\"segment\":\"a40\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons, and only one of them is the cap described above; the other two have nothing to do with how much traffic a caller has sent in the window it is currently in.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b39.\"},{\"segment\":\"b38\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons, and only one of them is the cap described above; the other two have nothing to do with how much traffic a caller has sent in the window it is currently in.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a40.\"},{\"segment\":\"b39\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons, and only one of them is the cap described above; the other two have nothing to do with how much traffic a caller has sent in the window it is currently in.\",\"reason\":\"Carried in merged sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"a41\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit, in which case it is refused before it has been read at all.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b40's refused-before-read detail.\"},{\"segment\":\"b40\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit, in which case it is refused before it has been read at all.\",\"reason\":\"Repair/maintenance same; unread-body detail kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"a43\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The distinction matters more to a retry loop than it does to a reader.\",\"reason\":\"b41's fuller comparison used.\"},{\"segment\":\"b41\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The distinction matters more to a retry loop than it does to a reader.\",\"reason\":\"'Difference' changed to base's 'distinction'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a44\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service, and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals and no successes, which reads like an outage and is not one; the wasted budget is the caller’s own.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b43.\"},{\"segment\":\"b42\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service, and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals and no successes, which reads like an outage and is not one; the wasted budget is the caller’s own.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a44.\"},{\"segment\":\"b43\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service, and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals and no successes, which reads like an outage and is not one; the wasted budget is the caller’s own.\",\"reason\":\"Outage-lookalike and own-budget details carried.\"},{\"segment\":\"a47\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A cap can be raised, but not on the strength of an assertion that the current one is too small: the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b46.\"},{\"segment\":\"b46\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A cap can be raised, but not on the strength of an assertion that the current one is too small: the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0.\",\"reason\":\"Moved to the increase section and merged with a47.\"},{\"segment\":\"a48\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Bring the refusal counts for a full week, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\",\"reason\":\"Uses b47's 'full week' phrasing.\"},{\"segment\":\"b47\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Bring the refusal counts for a full week, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\",\"reason\":\"Same list as a48.\"},{\"segment\":\"a49\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty before it looks at the number at all; a burst is cheaper to smooth out than it is to serve at its peak.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b48's ordering detail.\"},{\"segment\":\"b48\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty before it looks at the number at all; a burst is cheaper to smooth out than it is to serve at its peak.\",\"reason\":\"Before-the-number detail carried.\"},{\"segment\":\"b49\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty before it looks at the number at all; a burst is cheaper to smooth out than it is to serve at its peak.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a49.\"},{\"segment\":\"a50\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all. That is the cheapest fix available to anybody, it is available to almost everybody, and it is the outcome everyone prefers.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b45.\"},{\"segment\":\"b44\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a50.\"},{\"segment\":\"b45\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"That is the cheapest fix available to anybody, it is available to almost everybody, and it is the outcome everyone prefers.\",\"reason\":\"Carried with a50's closing clause.\"},{\"segment\":\"a51\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel and are answered within two working days.\",\"reason\":\"Tightened wording.\"},{\"segment\":\"b50\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel and are answered within two working days.\",\"reason\":\"Same channel fact as a51.\"},{\"segment\":\"b52\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel and are answered within two working days. There is no expedited path and no exception list, and chasing an answer does not make it arrive any sooner.\",\"reason\":\"Response time and no-chasing point carried.\"},{\"segment\":\"a52\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"There is no expedited path and no exception list, and chasing an answer does not make it arrive any sooner.\",\"reason\":\"Merged with b52's chasing point.\"},{\"segment\":\"